---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Overline from "../../components/brand/Overline.astro";
import Highlight from "../../components/brand/Highlight.astro";
import Button from "../../components/brand/Button.astro";
import { getRoute } from "../../i18n/utils";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
const modeloUrl = base + getRoute("modelo", "en");
---
<BaseLayout
  routeKey="diaDespues"
  title="The day after"
  description="On 10 August 2026 a magnitude 7.4 earthquake struck the Colombian department with the highest monetary poverty rate. What happens over the next two years matters more than what happened in the first two weeks."
>
  <section class="ground-green section dda-hero">
    <div class="container">
      <Overline tone="dark">The day after</Overline>
      <h1 class="display dda-hero__t">What saves lives doesn't arrive in the <Highlight variant="dark">emergency.</Highlight></h1>
      <p class="dda-hero__l">
        On 10 August 2026, a magnitude 7.4 earthquake centred on San José del Palmar struck the Colombian
        department with the highest monetary poverty rate in the country. This page doesn't ask for money.
        It explains why we exist.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ground-paper section">
    <div class="container dda">
      <p class="dda__k">Act one</p>
      <h2 class="display dda__h">Armenia already taught us the answer.</h2>
      <p class="dda__p">
        On 25 January 1999, a magnitude 6.2 earthquake destroyed the city of Armenia, Colombia. It killed
        921 people and collapsed more than 35,000 buildings. The whole country mobilised: donations,
        convoys, shelters.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p">
        On 10 August 2026, a <strong>magnitude 7.4</strong> quake — far stronger — shook the same city again.
        <strong>Nobody died. Not one building was reduced to rubble.</strong>
      </p>
      <blockquote class="dda__q">
        <p>“We're better prepared now… we had no deaths and no building ended up as rubble.”</p>
        <cite>Uriel Orjuela, president of the Quindío Society of Engineers · El País, 16 August 2026</cite>
      </blockquote>
      <p class="dda__p">
        The difference wasn't the aid that arrived in January 1999. It was the <strong>27 years that
        followed</strong>: seismic building codes, mandatory technical oversight, sustained rebuilding. Slow,
        invisible work with no cameras on it. That's what saved lives.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p dda__p--em">
        What saves lives isn't what arrives in the emergency. It's what is sustained once the emergency stops
        being news.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ground-ink section">
    <div class="container dda dda--dark">
      <p class="dda__k">Act two</p>
      <h2 class="display dda__h">Moravia is the day after that Colombia never attended to.</h2>
      <p class="dda__p">
        The neighbourhood where we work didn't appear by accident. From the 1960s it was settled by families
        displaced by rural violence who ended up building shacks on top of Medellín's municipal rubbish dump.
        By 1983 some 17,000 people lived there in extreme precarity.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p">
        Nobody called that an emergency. It was the accumulated result of many emergencies that were attended
        to for a few weeks and then forgotten.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p dda__p--em">
        We're not changing the subject. We work inside the ending of this film.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ground-paper section">
    <div class="container dda">
      <p class="dda__k">Act three</p>
      <h2 class="display dda__h">Chocó was already in the trap before 10 August.</h2>
      <div class="dda__stats">
        <div class="dstat"><span class="dstat__v">65.3%</span><span class="dstat__l">of Chocó's population lives in monetary poverty — the highest rate in Colombia. The national average is 28.0%.</span></div>
        <div class="dstat"><span class="dstat__v">44.3%</span><span class="dstat__l">live in extreme monetary poverty: 4.6 times the national average.</span></div>
        <div class="dstat"><span class="dstat__v">94%</span><span class="dstat__l">of people living in Chocó households with three or more children under 12 are in poverty.</span></div>
      </div>
      <p class="dda__p">
        But the figure that best describes a poverty trap is a different one. Between 2024 and 2025, extreme
        poverty in Colombia fell by 2.1 percentage points. <strong>In Chocó it barely moved — 0.6 points</strong>
        — a change the national statistics office itself does not consider statistically significant. And its
        Gini coefficient, the highest in the country, didn't fall by a single hundredth.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p dda__p--em">
        The whole country improved and Chocó stood still. That was before the earthquake.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__src">Source: DANE, Monetary Poverty 2025, departmental results, published 12 August 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="ground-paper-100 section">
    <div class="container dda">
      <p class="dda__k">What comes next</p>
      <h2 class="display dda__h">Where we fit into all of this.</h2>
      <p class="dda__p">
        We are not a disaster-response organisation and we won't pretend to be one. In the first weeks what
        saves lives is search and rescue, clean water, medical care and shelter — none of which you buy with
        a monthly transfer. That's what the Red Cross, the national risk agency and the teams already on the
        ground on 10 August are for.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p">
        Our work starts when theirs ends. The international evidence is consistent: <strong>two thirds of
        everything that will be donated after a disaster has already been given by the second month, and by
        month six giving has stopped.</strong> Rebuilding, meanwhile, takes four to six years. That gap is
        where a family decides whether to sell the tool they work with, or whether a girl leaves school.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p">
        Our model — a sustained monthly income, with support, for women heading households — is built for
        that gap. Today it operates in Moravia. <strong>And we are going to direct part of what we raise to
        Chocó.</strong>
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p dda__p--em">
        We are not going to run our own operation there, and we want to explain why.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p">
        In the worst-hit parts of the San Juan river basin markets are not functioning, several communities
        can only be reached by river, and there are security risks an organisation our size cannot manage
        alone. The World Food Programme — with vastly greater resources than ours — reached the same
        conclusion: it is delivering food, not cash, in Chocó's remote communities, precisely because
        without a functioning market money buys nothing.
      </p>
      <p class="dda__p">
        What we can do is <strong>fund those already there</strong>. An organisation with a permanent
        presence in the territory has what we lack: people who live there, acceptance built over years, and
        the real ability to reach communities. We bring what we know how to do: the sustained monthly income
        model, and the accounting for it.
      </p>
      <div class="dda__pledge reveal">
        <h3 class="dda__ph">Three commitments about that money</h3>
        <ol class="dda__pl">
          <li><strong>Money marked for Chocó is only spent in Chocó.</strong> Separate account, statement published monthly, naming the partner organisation and the number of households reached.</li>
          <li><strong>No existing contribution is reallocated without permission.</strong> If you're already a member, your contribution stays where it is unless you decide otherwise.</li>
          <li><strong>We raise nothing for emergency relief.</strong> The Red Cross and the national risk agency are there for that — which is why we link to them above rather than compete with them.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="dda__cta">
        <Button href={modeloUrl} variant="dark" size="lg">How the model works →</Button>
      </div>
      <p class="dda__src">
        Sources: Center for High Impact Philanthropy, University of Pennsylvania (post-disaster giving curve) ·
        reconstruction estimates reported in the Colombian national press, August 2026 · DANE, 2025 ·
        Colombian Geological Survey.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .dda-hero__t { font-size: clamp(30px, 5.5vw, 52px); color: var(--ink-900); max-width: 18ch; margin-top: 14px; line-height: 1.08; padding-bottom: 0.1em; }
  .dda-hero__l { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(16px, 2.1vw, 19px); line-height: 1.55; color: var(--ink-900); opacity: 0.82; max-width: 58ch; margin-top: 18px; }
  .dda { max-width: 720px; }
  .dda__k { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-weight: 700; font-size: 11.5px; letter-spacing: 0.12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--green-700); margin: 0; }
  .dda--dark .dda__k { color: var(--green-400); }
  .dda__h { font-size: clamp(26px, 4vw, 38px); color: var(--text-strong); max-width: 22ch; margin-top: 12px; line-height: 1.15; padding-bottom: 0.1em; }
  .dda--dark .dda__h { color: var(--paper-50); }
  .dda__p { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 500; font-size: clamp(15px, 2vw, 17.5px); line-height: 1.65; color: var(--text-body); margin-top: 18px; }
  .dda--dark .dda__p { color: var(--text-on-dark-muted); }
  .dda__p strong { font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-strong); }
  .dda--dark .dda__p strong { color: var(--paper-50); }
  .dda__p--em { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(18px, 2.6vw, 24px); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--text-strong); margin-top: 26px; }
  .dda--dark .dda__p--em { color: var(--paper-50); }
  .dda__q { margin: 26px 0 0; border-left: 4px solid var(--green-400); padding-left: 20px; }
  .dda__q p { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 800; font-size: clamp(17px, 2.4vw, 21px); line-height: 1.35; color: var(--text-strong); }
  .dda__q cite { display: block; font-family: var(--font-mono); font-style: normal; font-size: 11.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-faint); margin-top: 12px; }
  .dda__stats { display: grid; gap: 16px; margin-top: 28px; }
  .dstat { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 128px 1fr; gap: 18px; align-items: start; padding: 16px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--paper-200); }
  .dstat__v { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 900; font-size: clamp(30px, 5vw, 40px); line-height: 1; color: var(--green-700); letter-spacing: -0.02em; }
  .dstat__l { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 500; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.55; color: var(--text-body); }
  .dda__pledge { background: var(--paper-0); border: 1px solid var(--paper-200); border-left: 4px solid var(--green-400); border-radius: var(--radius-md); box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm); padding: 26px; margin-top: 30px; }
  .dda__ph { font-family: var(--font-display); font-weight: 800; font-size: 19px; color: var(--text-strong); }
  .dda__pl { margin: 14px 0 0; padding-left: 20px; display: grid; gap: 12px; }
  .dda__pl li { font-family: var(--font-body); font-weight: 500; font-size: 14.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-body); }
  .dda__pl strong { font-weight: 800; color: var(--text-strong); }
  .dda__cta { margin-top: 30px; }
  .dda__src { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 11px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--text-faint); margin-top: 26px; }
  @media (max-width: 620px) { .dstat { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 6px; } }
</style>
